\section*{The cohomological Hikita isomorphism for quivers}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
The equivariant cohomological Hikita correspondence is claimed for arbitrary finite quivers under the stated free stable-action hypothesis, as an algebra isomorphism preserving nilpotent structure. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 044, 2026-09-24): Correspondences first identify cohomology with an intermediate algebra using the full topological torus and its coefficient maps. A separate stable-pair and Laurent comparison identifies the stability-cocharacter fixed scheme with that same algebra; keeping scheme-theoretic quotients throughout retains nilpotents and empty cases.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
